Rationale for the choices:
- **8 experts / top-2 / c=1.25** — the Mixtral-style sweet spot: top-2 keeps routing quality and model capacity, c=1.25 allows ~25% load slack for token clustering without heavy dropping.
- **H=2048, L=24, ffn=2704** — 1.0B activated params (embeddings 65M + attention 403M + 24×(2×11.1M) experts) = 1B dense-equivalent; 2.6B total stored params is the expected ~2.6× overhead of 8-expert top-2.
- **EP=8, TP=1, DP=32** — one expert per GPU makes all-to-all a pure 8-rank exchange; at 2.6B params TP is unnecessary, so DP absorbs all 256 GPUs for throughput.
- **Memory ~30GB / 80GB** — leaves room for larger micro-batches or sequence-length scaling without KV-cache or recompute pressure.

